nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" 13194139534708 false] [17592186304684 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304685 13194139534708 true] [17592186304684 1089 "q-104467" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534708 true] [17592186304684 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304684 1113 #uuid "5046e0c1-2f8b-58f5-a21d-913e91899338" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304684 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-1(x-(-5))(x-(-4))(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3) & =-({x}^{2}+9x+20)(x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}+27x+20x+60) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304686 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304687 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304688 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304689 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304690 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1041 "selection" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304690 13194139534708 true] [17592186304685 1110 #uuid "753ec0e2-b325-5183-8e84-914a8d2e5340" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304686 1034 "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-19x+30" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304686 1111 #uuid "f7d017c2-e3ff-56d9-9334-9ac4fa843657" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304687 1034 "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-38x-30" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304687 1111 #uuid "3c61eea0-6b09-573a-b969-b636455c3741" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304688 1034 "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+47x+60" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304688 1111 #uuid "151c154c-d125-5381-9ace-152bee787a80" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304689 1034 "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+19x+60" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304689 1111 #uuid "e58c95f7-87e5-56a0-956d-88829d4e8f33" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304690 1034 "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304690 1111 #uuid "1ceb7ee0-935f-5b83-9144-6119f5574980" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304692 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1089 "q-107669" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1100 "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 5\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $f(x).$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1113 #uuid "3f062701-62d1-5aa3-83ee-10a91ad72608" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304691 1145 "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304693 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304694 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304695 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304696 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304697 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1041 "selection" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304695 13194139534708 true] [17592186304692 1110 #uuid "94559dc5-1453-5aed-9198-b151af7188a3" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304693 1034 "2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+10" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304693 1111 #uuid "8304950d-6419-57c7-9abe-14caec07459d" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304694 1034 "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+20x-15" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304694 1111 #uuid "908682db-2b13-5c2b-bf37-704b0d1db340" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304695 1034 "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304695 1111 #uuid "3f46aa04-1eae-5968-925a-f7fde1628daf" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304696 1034 "{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+150" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304696 1111 #uuid "381bf829-01de-5bda-b8ca-3b1a094b4d6c" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304697 1034 "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304697 1111 #uuid "7eb85c7a-b314-5c83-b299-1b58b61fea34" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304699 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1089 "q-107670" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/a926400e24bc00ca9027d44461e800fa22015ff8289f05fba3a8b51f8b72cce5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1113 #uuid "78253fad-7e11-5fbb-92d7-9defd14f1c64" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304698 1145 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(2-2\\text{i})-x(2+2\\text{i})+(2+2\\text{i})(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4x+8) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304700 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304701 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304702 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304703 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304704 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1041 "selection" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304703 13194139534708 true] [17592186304699 1110 #uuid "7d86a62f-bd17-5303-ba04-3f9325c1e31c" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304700 1034 "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+16x" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304700 1111 #uuid "af094840-468d-54c0-b013-c15534112a19" 13194139534708 tr