9a.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304712 1113 #uuid "30239ac5-d2ec-5338-817c-8dbb2bd8190d" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304712 1145 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-x(2-3\\text{i})-x(2+3\\text{i})+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-4x+13) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+13x-3{x}^{2}+12x-39 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39.$" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304714 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304715 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304716 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304717 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304718 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1041 "selection" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304717 13194139534708 true] [17592186304713 1110 #uuid "a0b69fc7-7644-53a8-9834-af1d6c37a7db" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304714 1034 "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-13" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534708 true] [17592186304714 1111 #uuid "3b56a55e-d4af-5687-91dc-04572d49c2b5" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304715 1034 "{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-36" 13194139534708 true] [17592186304715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045